Data files that ship, their source and their licence

  extension/rules/*.json
      Written by this project. CC BY-SA 4.0.
  extension/data/outlets.json
      Compiled by hand by this project from public sources, most of them Wikipedia
      (CC BY-SA). Each row links its sources. CC BY-SA 4.0.
  extension/data/owners.json
      Built from Wikidata by scripts/build-owners.py. Wikidata's data is CC0.
  extension/data/sec-tickers.json
      Built from the US Securities and Exchange Commission's public list of company tickers
      by scripts/build-sec-tickers.js. A work of the US government, in the public domain.
  extension/data/stat-series.json
      Written by this project: a list of official statistical series and their ids.
      CC BY-SA 4.0. The statistics themselves are fetched from their publishers at run time.
  extension/data/category-playbook.json
      Researched and written by this project, with links to the pages described and short
      quotations from them. CC BY-SA 4.0. The quoted words belong to their publishers.
  data/lists/*.json, data/reliability-ledger.json
      Written by this project. CC BY-SA 4.0.

Data files that are not in the public copy

  Some data files are held out of the public copy until their licences or contents have
  been reviewed. docs/PUBLISHING.md lists them. A copy that does include
  extension/data/known-bad.json must also include extension/data/GPL-3.0.txt,
  extension/data/COI-open-data-licence.txt and extension/data/NOTICE-lists.md, which
  credit its sources and carry their licence texts.

Third-party software

  Playwright (Apache-2.0) is used for tests only and is not distributed with the extension.
